# FCSpreadSheet2 — Project file

## Description
A FreeCAD spreadsheet workbench (Python addon) similar to the default
FreeCAD Spreadsheet workbench. It reuses FreeCAD's built-in
`Spreadsheet::Sheet` objects through a thin Python wrapper and exposes a
custom workbench with toolbar/menu commands.

## Tech stack
- FreeCAD 1.x / 2.x (AppImages at `~/Applications/`)
- Python 3.11 (bundled with FreeCAD)
- Namespace workbench structure: `freecad/fcspreadsheet2/`
- Addon Manager metadata via `package.xml`

## Architecture
- `freecad/fcspreadsheet2/__init__.py` — headless entry (exports `__version__`)
- `freecad/fcspreadsheet2/version.py` — `__version__`
- `freecad/fcspreadsheet2/init_gui.py` — GUI entry: registers icons, translations, commands, workbench
- `freecad/fcspreadsheet2/workbench.py` — `FCSpreadSheet2Workbench` (Gui.Workbench)
- `freecad/fcspreadsheet2/commands/` — command classes (toolbar/menu actions)
- `freecad/fcspreadsheet2/sheet.py` — `Sheet` wrapper around `Spreadsheet::Sheet`
- `freecad/fcspreadsheet2/resources/` — icons + translations + `Resources` manager

## Install / dev loop
- Dev (no install): `~/Applications/FreeCAD_1.1.3-Linux-x86_64-py311.AppImage -M ~/projects/FCSpreadSheet2`
- Or symlink: `ln -s ~/projects/FCSpreadSheet2 ~/.local/share/FreeCAD/Mod/FCSpreadSheet2`
- Headless tests: extract AppImage once, then
  `./squashfs-root/AppRun freecadcmd -M ~/projects/FCSpreadSheet2 tests/test_sheet.py`

## Notes / decisions
- License: LGPL-2.1-or-later (same as FreeCAD)
- Maintainer: Chris (email placeholder)
- Cell read API: use `Sheet.getContents(address)` for raw cell content;
  `Sheet.get(address)` only returns cells exposed as properties, so the
  `Sheet` wrapper routes `get()` through `getContents()`.

## Plan
The detailed technical plan lives in `PLAN.md`. Core idea: a single **MasterSheet**
per project (reusable across files), and a per-part **ConfigRef** that links to it
and selects a named row, so many parts share one spreadsheet without copying it.

